{"id":"sl/y90nupkv","index":0,"title":"Rust Loop Vectorizer for LLVM 21","elements":[{"id":"im/4fi1k7eh","kind":"image","position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/k3yl0zql","kind":"textbox","text":"Rust Loop Vectorizer for LLVM 21","position":{"left":549.43,"top":236.45,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/7qp4be9c","kind":"textbox","text":"A correctness-first compiler pass and project-scale vectorization CLI","position":{"left":549.43,"top":296.09,"width":661.09,"height":54.27},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/65g3298r","kind":"textbox","text":"The project transforms safe scalar loops into LLVM vector IR and provides tools to run, inspect, and verify vectorization across a codebase. It emphasizes correctness, explainable decisions, and reproducible evaluation while offering textual IR, bitcode, and object emission for integration with real builds.","position":{"left":549.43,"top":375.19,"width":661.09,"height":111.13},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/hwbqtkby","index":1,"title":"The Problem and Project Goal","elements":[{"id":"im/kbq1c3i1","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/ozy1ofad","kind":"textbox","text":"The Problem and Project Goal","position":{"left":69.45,"top":165.6,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/b29kza94","kind":"textbox","text":"Scalar loops process one element per iteration even when hardware provides SIMD units. Automatic vectorization must prove that reordering or grouping iterations is safe. This project combines a deliberately conservative Rust vectorization pass with LLVM 21 tooling to ensure correct, explainable, and practically integrable transformations across projects, with reproducible evaluation.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":243.13,"width":661.09,"height":138.91},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/a10jqpsj","kind":"shape","position":{"left":69.45,"top":401.56,"width":321.87,"height":155.6}},{"id":"sh/x4r21kru","kind":"textbox","text":"Primary Goals","position":{"left":86.8,"top":418.92,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/w3i1sfa9","kind":"textbox","text":"Correct transformations, explainable decisions, practical project integration, reproducible evaluation.","position":{"left":86.8,"top":456.47,"width":287.16,"height":83.34},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/r65knqtk","kind":"shape","position":{"left":408.67,"top":401.56,"width":321.87,"height":155.6}},{"id":"sh/q5wjelsz","kind":"textbox","text":"Design Stance","position":{"left":426.02,"top":418.92,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ove9o7yd","kind":"textbox","text":"Conservative legality first, accept only provably safe changes; provide diagnostics when rejecting.","position":{"left":426.02,"top":456.47,"width":287.16,"height":83.34},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/ofy9wn61","index":2,"title":"System Architecture","elements":[{"id":"im/h0vmtcz2","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/d0jax03i","kind":"textbox","text":"System Architecture","position":{"left":69.45,"top":239.28,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/298ryl4v","kind":"textbox","text":"Inputs include LLVM IR/bitcode, supported source files, compilation databases, or build-produced IR manifests. A small C++ bridge registers the plugin with LLVM's New Pass Manager and exposes selected APIs. Rust handles loop discovery, legality checks, dependence analysis, profitability planning, IR construction, and diagnostics. LLVM verifies results; the CLI writes textual IR, bitcode, or objects. An optional hybrid mode runs LLVM’s production Loop Vectorizer after the Rust pass.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":316.8,"width":661.09,"height":166.69},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/jyx0ra1s","index":3,"title":"What the Rust Pass Vectorizes","elements":[{"id":"im/ozat8bi1","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/0ba143al","kind":"textbox","text":"What the Rust Pass Vectorizes","position":{"left":69.45,"top":163.6,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/rm1k7yt4","kind":"textbox","text":"The pass discovers canonical, single-block, count-up loops and handles contiguous loads/stores of i8, i16, i32, i64, half, float, and double. It widens arithmetic, shifts, bitwise ops, casts, comparisons, and select into fixed-width vector IR while preserving the original scalar path for short inputs and remainders. The CLI supports vector factors 2, 4, 8, and 16.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":241.13,"width":661.09,"height":138.91},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ql8jytsj","kind":"shape","position":{"left":69.45,"top":399.56,"width":321.87,"height":159.6}},{"id":"sh/doj29oba","kind":"textbox","text":"Supported Patterns","position":{"left":88.8,"top":418.92,"width":283.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/sna103ap","kind":"textbox","text":"Single-block counted loops with contiguous memory accesses and supported element types.","position":{"left":88.8,"top":456.47,"width":283.16,"height":83.34},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/3ihk3et8","kind":"shape","position":{"left":408.67,"top":399.56,"width":321.87,"height":159.6}},{"id":"sh/ih8ju9sn","kind":"textbox","text":"Vector Widths","position":{"left":428.02,"top":418.92,"width":283.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/kbm987y5","kind":"textbox","text":"CLI-configurable vector factors: 2, 4, 8, 16; scalar fallback for tails.","position":{"left":428.02,"top":456.47,"width":283.16,"height":55.56},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/i107q5of","index":4,"title":"Safety and Vectorization Decisions","elements":[{"id":"im/8jatkbq9","kind":"image","position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/cf2tcr61","kind":"textbox","text":"Safety and Vectorization Decisions","position":{"left":549.43,"top":124.58,"width":661.09,"height":108.5},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/z2tcnm5s","kind":"textbox","text":"Loops are rejected if control flow, memory access, data layout, or dependencies cannot be proved safe. The pass checks affine memory indices, same-base dependence distances, and conservative alias relationships. A forced vector width never bypasses legality checks. Profitability policies available: conservative, balanced, and aggressive.","position":{"left":549.43,"top":256.35,"width":661.09,"height":138.91},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/yhkbe1o7","kind":"shape","position":{"left":549.43,"top":414.79,"width":321.87,"height":183.39}},{"id":"sh/l4bupwny","kind":"textbox","text":"Target Info","position":{"left":566.79,"top":432.15,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/032tgr6d","kind":"textbox","text":"Uses LLVM target info for register-width selection when a target triple is declared; otherwise defaults to a 128-bit baseline.","position":{"left":566.79,"top":469.7,"width":287.16,"height":111.13},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/n6dcr65o","kind":"shape","position":{"left":888.65,"top":414.79,"width":321.87,"height":183.39}},{"id":"sh/m5kbi1oj","kind":"textbox","text":"Reporting","position":{"left":906.01,"top":432.15,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/w32dkbuh","kind":"textbox","text":"Reports acceptance/rejection reasons, selected vector factor, estimated coverage, and analysis/transformation time.","position":{"left":906.01,"top":469.7,"width":287.16,"height":111.13},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/x8f69ofe","index":5,"title":"Whole-Project and Multi-Language Inputs","elements":[{"id":"im/vmp43mlo","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/zi98nu94","kind":"textbox","text":"Whole-Project and Multi-Language Inputs","position":{"left":69.45,"top":105.8,"width":661.09,"height":108.5},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/87ipkzal","kind":"textbox","text":"The CLI recursively processes a project folder, mirroring source paths in the output directory and producing one LLVM module per translation unit. Built-in adapters support C, C++, Objective-C, Objective-C++, Fortran, Rust, and Swift when toolchains are available. Language-independent integration requires frontends to produce LLVM 21-compatible IR or bitcode; the CLI does not compile every language natively.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":237.57,"width":661.09,"height":138.91},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"im/8jyl8rmd","kind":"image","position":{"left":69.45,"top":396.01,"width":43.41,"height":43.41}},{"id":"sh/ml07i9sv","kind":"textbox","text":"Frontend Options","position":{"left":134.55,"top":396.01,"width":595.99,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/7m98ru9g","kind":"textbox","text":"--frontend-config to add compilers; --input-manifest accepts externally produced LLVM IR/bitcode.","position":{"left":134.55,"top":433.56,"width":595.99,"height":55.56},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"im/lwn2dc3m","kind":"image","position":{"left":69.45,"top":523.84,"width":43.41,"height":43.41}},{"id":"sh/pc76hkr2","kind":"textbox","text":"Build DB","position":{"left":134.55,"top":523.84,"width":595.99,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/h4bupgn6","kind":"textbox","text":"--compile-commands reuses Clang flags, working dirs, includes, defines, and target settings from a compilation database.","position":{"left":134.55,"top":561.4,"width":595.99,"height":55.56},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/gnmp4jqx","index":6,"title":"Engines and Output Choices","elements":[{"id":"im/hojmp072","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/dcbud0ra","kind":"textbox","text":"Engines and Output Choices","position":{"left":69.45,"top":151.7,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ydkbm5sv","kind":"textbox","text":"Engine modes: --engine rust (Rust-only conservative pass), --engine hybrid (Rust pass then LLVM Loop Vectorizer for broader cases), and --engine llvm (LLVM Loop Vectorizer alone). Target-aware planning and object emission are configured via --target-triple, --cpu, and --features. Outputs include readable .ll, LLVM .bc, or linkable .o files; the CLI emits one object per module and relies on the native build system for linking.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":229.23,"width":661.09,"height":166.69},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/zedcfa9g","kind":"shape","position":{"left":69.45,"top":415.45,"width":321.87,"height":155.6}},{"id":"sh/kzmdova1","kind":"textbox","text":"Engine Choices","position":{"left":86.8,"top":432.8,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/l0vuh0rm","kind":"textbox","text":"rust | hybrid | llvm — tradeoffs between conservative correctness and broader LLVM coverage.","position":{"left":86.8,"top":470.35,"width":287.16,"height":83.34},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/eh0ba1sr","kind":"shape","position":{"left":408.67,"top":415.45,"width":321.87,"height":155.6}},{"id":"sh/fi9c369c","kind":"textbox","text":"Outputs","position":{"left":426.02,"top":432.8,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/baxkjqlk","kind":"textbox","text":".ll (text), .bc (bitcode), .o (object files via --emit-object).","position":{"left":426.02,"top":470.35,"width":287.16,"height":55.56},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/fu1gfa1s","index":7,"title":"Developer Experience & Large-Project Operation","elements":[{"id":"im/8rah0by9","kind":"image","position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/g72x4zyd","kind":"textbox","text":"Developer Experience & Large-Project Operation","position":{"left":549.43,"top":117.85,"width":661.09,"height":108.5},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ri9g7uhw","kind":"shape","position":{"left":536.93,"top":249.62,"width":334.37,"height":355.28}},{"id":"sh/6h0fypgb","kind":"textbox","text":"Insight (Diagnostics & UI)","position":{"left":554.29,"top":268.2,"width":299.66,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#000000","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/tkby9kzm","kind":"textbox","text":"Text and JSON diagnostics include per-file status, Rust loop decisions, optional source locations, LLVM remarks, and toolchain details. --doctor validates LLVM tools, plugin loading, and optional frontends. A terminal UI provides editable paths, policy/width controls, and a scrollable results pane for inspection.","position":{"left":554.29,"top":311.47,"width":299.66,"height":250.03},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#000000","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/sjix0zy1","kind":"textbox","text":"Automation & Safeguards","position":{"left":901.82,"top":268.2,"width":309.37,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/je9g3ahk","kind":"textbox","text":"--jobs processes independent modules concurrently. --cache-dir reuses content-verified artifacts when dependencies are known. Time, memory, and input-size limits bound work. --fail-on-missed gates Rust-pass rejections; --compare-config compares baseline and candidate outputs with optional runtime thresholds. Atomic output publication preserves previous artifacts on failure.","position":{"left":901.82,"top":311.47,"width":309.37,"height":277.81},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/udsvah03","index":8,"title":"Verification and Measured Results","elements":[{"id":"im/gn614nex","kind":"image","position":{"left":799.98,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/0b65obm9","kind":"textbox","text":"Verification and Measured Results","position":{"left":69.45,"top":96.8,"width":661.09,"height":108.5},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/nex4jq5k","kind":"textbox","text":"Verification includes Rust tests, CLI/project integration tests, LLVM's verifier, native correctness harnesses, and rejection fixtures. A quick generated differential suite executed 8,192 runs. In a recorded local seven-kernel benchmark all scalar, custom-pass, and LLVM variants passed correctness.","position":{"left":69.45,"top":228.57,"width":661.09,"height":111.13},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/mdonql4z","kind":"shape","position":{"left":69.45,"top":359.23,"width":321.87,"height":266.73}},{"id":"sh/9gzml0nq","kind":"textbox","text":"Speedup (local benchmark)","position":{"left":86.8,"top":376.58,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ofq5svm5","kind":"textbox","text":"Geometric-mean versus scalar: custom Rust pass 3.009×; LLVM Loop Vectorizer 2.974×.","position":{"left":86.8,"top":414.14,"width":287.16,"height":83.34},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/bih4na5w","kind":"shape","position":{"left":408.67,"top":359.23,"width":321.87,"height":266.73}},{"id":"sh/ah8nu54b","kind":"textbox","text":"Compile-Time Corpus","position":{"left":426.02,"top":376.58,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/oza1gfyh","kind":"textbox","text":"On a 128-loop corpus the custom pass transformed 128/128 loops; median in-pass analysis+transform time: 2.355 µs per cloned loop. Footnote: local cache-hot measurements on Apple M5 with LLVM 21.1.3 — not universal claims.","position":{"left":426.02,"top":414.14,"width":287.16,"height":194.47},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}
{"id":"sl/m90b6t0r","index":9,"title":"Scope, Strengths, and Next Steps","elements":[{"id":"im/kvy9wvmx","kind":"image","position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":479.99,"height":720}},{"id":"sh/cbu58j2h","kind":"textbox","text":"Scope, Strengths, and Next Steps","position":{"left":549.43,"top":137.82,"width":661.09,"height":54.25},"style":{"fontSize":43.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#F3F3F2","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/zelojyl8","kind":"textbox","text":"Strengths: real vector IR generation, conservative correctness checks, explainable loop decisions, project-scale inputs, multiple output formats, and automated verification. The Rust pass intentionally supports a bounded loop subset; unsupported shapes remain scalar under that engine. Hybrid and LLVM modes extend coverage using LLVM’s production vectorizer — those transformations are performed by LLVM, not the Rust pass.","position":{"left":549.43,"top":215.34,"width":661.09,"height":166.69},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/ydcnatkn","kind":"shape","position":{"left":549.43,"top":401.56,"width":321.87,"height":183.39}},{"id":"sh/l036l83y","kind":"textbox","text":"Future Research","position":{"left":566.79,"top":418.92,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/kzu5c32t","kind":"textbox","text":"Richer target throughput costing, scalable vectors, masked tails, interleaving, and expanded Rust-pass legality proofs.","position":{"left":566.79,"top":456.47,"width":287.16,"height":111.13},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/725onyl4","kind":"shape","position":{"left":888.65,"top":401.56,"width":321.87,"height":183.39}},{"id":"sh/m1cnetkj","kind":"textbox","text":"Closing Line","position":{"left":906.01,"top":418.92,"width":287.16,"height":27.14},"style":{"fontSize":21.33,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans Medium","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}},{"id":"sh/s7yt4b21","kind":"textbox","text":"Vectorize when safe. Explain when not. Integrate with real builds.","position":{"left":906.01,"top":456.47,"width":287.16,"height":55.56},"style":{"fontSize":17.33,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#D4D4D1","alignment":"left"}}]}